Yep, this is a difficult question.. sometimes when I encounter a recent
bones file, I may remember many of the items I died with.

But even if it's a very old file and I don't remember it (or if it's
somebody else's bones in a multiuser system), it is often possible to
recognize the character class from some items in the pile, and then some
other items may be recognized with an educated guess, especially if it is
an early-game level.

For example, if I see a Hawaiian shirt and a camera, but not very good
armor and no good weapons in a bones pile, I can be almost sure it is a
bones pile of a tourist. And if I see four scrolls of the same type, but
not many other scrolls, I can guess those are scrolls of magic mapping.
If I see a stethoscope and leather gloves and a scalpel in the pile, it is
almost certainly the grave of a healer. So, if there are two stacks of
potions, they are most likely healing and extra healing.
If there's a quarterstaff, a cloak, several spellbooks and no good weapons
and not much other armor, it is probably wizard and so the cloak is
probably magic protection. 

